#!args scenario=Scenario_AllCards seed=42
#
# Regression: a block reaction that pays a cost must still block.
#
# StatusRadar ("discard the top 2 cards of your draw deck and do not remove that Navy") applied its
# ForceDiscardCardsChangeEvent and *then* looked up its block target via
# CardPlayPool.LastNoneNewCardChangeEvent. But ChangeEvent.ApplyMutation registers every applied
# event into the round's ChangeEventsPool — IsTrigger=false suppresses the reaction chain, not the
# registration — so that read landed on the discard, the `is RemoveUnitChangeEvent` pattern failed
# silently, IsBlocked was never set, and the player paid 2 cards while the Navy was still removed.
#
# Step logic now reads CardLogic.ActivationTrigger, which DoCard pins to the event the card was
# activated against for the whole activation. The two assertions below are the two halves of the
# card: the cost IS paid (decksize 22 -> 20) AND the removal IS blocked (the Navy is still there).
# Without the fix the first holds and the second does not.
#
# This is the only test covering the block-reaction path at all.
#
# Run:  tests/run-cli.sh tests/qgc/block_reaction_prevents_removal.qgc

# The six mandatory opening discards, auto-answered — see opening_turn.qgc. This one is safe to
# auto-answer; the deliberate absence of an answer command further down is not.
auto 6

prompt                                  # turn 1, Germany — synchronise with the running game

# Scenario_AllCards already has StatusRadar in play for the US, but the US only starts with an Army
# in US East. Give it a Navy in the adjacent sea so Radar's "supplied Navy" trigger can match.
# `force` (IsTrigger=false) keeps the setup itself out of the reaction chain.
force deployUnit --faction UNITED_STATES --country NORTH_ATLANTIC --deploy BUILD
assert units NORTH_ATLANTIC UNITED_STATES == 1

# Deck composition, so re-derive after any change to QGData_Decks.json. Unit id 110 comes from the
# scenario's deployments and is not affected by the decks. Three lower than it used to be: the
# opening hand is dealt at OpeningHandSize rather than HandSize, and the three cards cut back come
# off the hand into the discard pile, not back into the deck.
assert decksize UNITED_STATES == 22

api removeUnit --faction JAPAN --unit 110 --reason BATTLE
pass                                    # UK declines Destroyers on the removal — this offer is correct
pass                                    # Soviet: always-ask window on the removal, no options
play 1                                  # US plays Radar

# Radar's activation opens its own block window, and the UK used to be offered Destroyers again
# inside it — a removal-blocker matching a card activation, because UnitAboutToBeRemoved read
# LastNoneNewCardChangeEvent (which skips ActivateReactionChangeEvent and so still reported the
# removal). Block triggers now match CurrentBlockTrigger, so nothing matches here.
#
# The UK is still ASKED: it holds a face-down Destroyers, and the always-ask rule
# (CardPlayRound.ShouldOpenReactionWindow) opens a window for every such faction so that being asked
# stops proving a card matched. So the regression signal is no longer "does a prompt appear" — it is
# "does that prompt carry any options". `assert promptoptions == 0` on the UK's window is the check;
# it FAILS (1) the moment Destroyers is wrongly offered against a card activation again.
pass                                    # block window on the activation: Japan  (no options)
pass                                    #                                Italy  (no options)
assert promptfaction == UNITED_KINGDOM  # the window that used to wrongly offer Destroyers
assert promptoptions == 0               # FAILS (1) if a removal-blocker matches an activation again
pass                                    #                                UK     (no options)
pass                                    #                                Soviet (no options)
pass                                    # activation window:             Japan  (no options)
pass                                    #                                Italy  (no options)
pass                                    #                                UK     (no options)
pass                                    #                                Soviet (no options)

assert units NORTH_ATLANTIC UNITED_STATES == 1   # FAILS (0) if the block was lost
assert decksize UNITED_STATES == 20              # the cost was still paid

quit
